Detect libc++ on QNX with GCC too, so std types are not forward-declared.

doctest forward-declares std::ostream, std::tuple, ... itself unless it
sees it is on libc++ (_LIBCPP_VERSION), and it includes <version>/<ciso646>
to find that out only when the compiler is clang. QNX's C++ library is
libc++ (its types live in std::__2) also with QNX's GCC, so with GCC the
forward declarations named a different std::tuple and every
TEST_CASE_TEMPLATE failed with "template argument 1 is invalid". Probe for
libc++ on QNX too.

Upstream-Status: Pending

--- a/doctest/doctest.h
+++ b/doctest/doctest.h
@@ -485,7 +485,7 @@
 // which case we don't want to forward declare stuff from std - for reference:
 // https://github.com/doctest/doctest/issues/126
 // https://github.com/doctest/doctest/issues/356
-#if DOCTEST_CLANG
+#if DOCTEST_CLANG || defined(__QNX__) // QNX: libc++ also with GCC
 #if DOCTEST_CPLUSPLUS >= 201703L && __has_include(<version>)
 #include <version>
 #else
--- a/doctest/parts/public/config.h
+++ b/doctest/parts/public/config.h
@@ -176,7 +176,7 @@
 // which case we don't want to forward declare stuff from std - for reference:
 // https://github.com/doctest/doctest/issues/126
 // https://github.com/doctest/doctest/issues/356
-#if DOCTEST_CLANG
+#if DOCTEST_CLANG || defined(__QNX__) // QNX: libc++ also with GCC
 #if DOCTEST_CPLUSPLUS >= 201703L && __has_include(<version>)
 #include <version>
 #else
